# Shared typed admission: boundary algebra and checked instances

`Machines.BoundaryCore.Protocol` separates entry, body, discharge and complete
batch selection over a carrier. The multiset and ordered-list specializations
share this definition. Their observers are not identified: ordered collection
does not factor through the answer bag.

## Checked instances

* `BoundaryProtocol`: the existing PeTTa row protocol, including shared guard
  stores and exact multiplicity; HE's actual return-boundary bag observation.
* `OrderedHEBoundary`: ordered HE return processing, retained completion
  frames, and the impossibility of forgetting an observable return range.
* `HEExpressionBoundary`: unconditional one-level factorization of the
  existing all-candidate HE expression worker, including all type rows,
  binding alternatives, tuple fallback and applicability diagnostics. Its
  source profile is explicit and is not native first-success execution.
* `RowAlphaInvariance`: canonical names give injective row renamings;
  complete guard-store bags and open-row calls are invariant.
* `ChainRegionAdmission`: actual equation expressions with checked activation
  boundaries, untyped non-tail calls and separately owed return classes.
* `HEConstructorAdmission`, `HEPreparedReturn`, `HEStructuralBoundary`:
  executable closed/single-applicability certificates derive constructor and
  argument self-delivery, matched-only calls with canonical fallback, and
  concrete shown-value return elision.
* `StampInference`: ordered first-match-per-argument inference, operational
  checking equivalence and validated transition caching. Matching and type
  normalization remain explicit services, not assumed native correspondence.
  `GroundStampMatcher` supplies arbitrary-variable ground structural matching,
  wildcard rules, row renaming and ground-only cache publication.
* `UnifyingRegions`: the existing expression syntax with substitution-carrying
  two-way binding outcomes; syntactic admission derives uninterpreted-version
  hypotheses for the unary recursive region.
* `RangeBoundary`, `RangeEvidence`, `HEOpenRangeTransport`: open-range
  equality requires agreement on its variable support. Retained ground typing
  observations can derive it; actual HE checks distinguish retained and reset
  records, including a polymorphic value with one declaration row.
* `TypedSquareCollection`: an actual typed square equation over every integer,
  its native multiplication service and a retained ordered collector. Every
  partial run preserves the source residual; its transition bound is an
  administrative model cost, not a native instruction bound.
* `ReturnPolicySeparation`: PeTTa's enclosing result guard and HE's nested
  return-policy replacement are observably different, even for Number and
  Undefined ranges. Object types are not interchangeable admission proofs.
* `FirstSuccessBoundary`: first-success selection and return processing are
  connected to the actual scoped HE worker, retaining caller stacks, emitted
  prefixes, bindings and suspension. Earned scoped derivations connect to
  source paths; external atom-branch realizations remain outside this profile.
* `ReadyConstructorBoundary`: once operands have been delivered, constructor
  restoration does not evaluate them again. Source head exclusion derives a
  complete candidate frontier; the scoped worker restores the ready node.
  Rejection by a post-build type check need not be a source-language error.
* `HESourceRegions`, `HERetainedConditional`: source-derived region plans and
  retained condition continuations preserve canonical results in their stated
  profiles. Computed conditions retain arbitrary outcomes and records; a
  non-Boolean result resumes the reached invocation rather than restarting it.
* `HEBindingConsumers`: the existing equality-aware projection preserves the
  complete retained read list. Full binding erasure is justified by the
  consumer, not by a ground returned value or replacement with unit.
* `HERawAdmission`: source argument applicability cannot in general be
  reconstructed from the delivered value alone. Its raw-lookup profile is
  explicit and is not the native recursive inferred-type service.
* `UnifyingFrames`, `RefinedUninterpreted`, `CapturedUninterpretedRegions`,
  `UninterpretedLocalMultiplicity`: actual two-way binding preserves frames
  whose instantiated support is disjoint. Recursive source lowering admits
  arbitrary ground pass-through frames, without global uniqueness of unrelated
  declarations, and preserves the complete canonical answer bag.
* `NativeTypeViews`: independent ordered source and descriptor traversals
  agree when the descriptor retains the question-qualified observations.
  Optional completed reads decline without forcing missing queries. Scoped
  retained-key correctness requires an explicit observation codec. The
  controls refute the older child-kind/full-type key on actual Atom fixtures.
* `HEMatchedReturnBoundary`: reached equation dispatch is another instance
  of the shared ordered boundary. Emitted function bodies run before the
  retained return receiver; matched empty results are not unmatched calls.
  Its derived optional delivery instantiates `HEDispatchDeopt.tiered_delivery`.
* `HEInvocationFrontier`: the existing three-class normalizer instantiated
  on complete HE result pairs. It preserves bindings and ordered duplicates
  while retiring fallback payloads after success. Its native output policy
  differs from the older binary model selection on mixed Empty batches;
  no operand/control-frontier equivalence is asserted.
* `NativeTypeDemand`: the actual ordered inference traversal is a read-only
  query plan. Admission consumes only available completed observations and
  declines at its first missing read. The exact read certificate permits
  reuse without forcing unused child queries.
* `NativeSymbolKeys`: symbol identity reconstructs both child observations;
  non-symbol inference needs its explicit tuple-view projection. The
  existing `StampKeys` table law follows from those primitive read contracts,
  rather than assuming whole inference congruence.
* `OpenFrameEffects`, `OpenFrameSourceAdmission`, `OpenFrameCertificate`:
  current-substitution scopes and executable source/return certificates
  derive recursive protocol equality with genuinely open disjoint captures.
  Indirect aliases and scope escapes are rejected. Native fact flags and
  hidden dependency ports require their own representation correspondence.
* `HEUniqueRangeGate`, `HESelectiveRangeGate`: actual applicability checks
  produce the selected record for arbitrary open formals. The computed
  formal/range sharing mask chooses uniqueness or first-success admission per
  position. This earns a scoped worker transition without assuming full call
  equality. Erasing private records during argument evaluation remains open.
* `HEMatchedCursorBoundary`: the matched-occurrence flag is derived from
  actual query/merge batches before producer execution. The typed unmatched
  close hands off, while matched empty bodies complete. This proves the local
  unmatched-provenance omission, not the recursive provenance analyzer.
* `Machines.RevisionedQueryWork`: the existing non-evicting cache computes
  once per distinct missing stamped key. `NativeSymbolKeys` instantiates
  that service-count law; key acquisition and native runtime costs are separate.
* `ValueRowInstances`: hereditary row-free values preserve exactly the first
  selected typing intersection in the existing ground-solution model. Private
  projection follows from separated source constraints, not names alone.
* `ContractBindingFacts`, `TrustedAliasControls`: the actual unifier preserves
  inherited and newly marked facts under current-dependency evidence. A
  functional declaration space and independent flag checks do not suffice:
  changing an aliased open head invalidates a discharged result guard, even
  when a caller ignores the value and observes only continuation execution.
* `GroundUninterpretedVersions`: every parameter in one two-way substitution
  and the C's name-level analysis. With the polymorphic argument ground and
  uninterpreted, the ground facts survive every binding and the version is the
  protocol at every fuel. Admitting an open argument where the other arguments
  are ground is refuted twice: a call's answer carries its variables to an
  unclaimed name, and a head pattern shares its variable with a ground one.
* `HEConstructorRecordDelivery`: the executable recursive constructor
  certificate earns actual evaluator delivery under an open caller expected
  type. The actual selected type-match record constructs the contextual frame
  and preserves its future covered observations. Its declaration profile is
  closed; schematic/native inferred-lookup correspondence is separate.
* `HESelectedCallComposition`: selected-function entry composes with an
  earned ordinary call, including absence. Operator/argument/call children
  derive the whole source judgment and checked worker run; no whole-expression
  run or nonempty equation assumption is added.
  `HEFunctionBranchComposition` extends the operator-result branch to arbitrary
  ordered operator results and child argument-packet batches, with each reached
  record and actual saved stack retained. `HEInvocationBranchComposition`
  executes the resulting call frontier and drains its activation tail.
  `HESelectedBranchDerivation.selected_from_components` composes these blocks
  with actual first-success entry, return readout, priority and publication;
  no whole-expression or whole-invocation run is an admission premise.
  Five-branch controls preserve duplicates, stopped results and distinct
  nonempty records. A source-earned typed constructor instantiates the full
  composed theorem. These are the existing checked plain-Atom worker's
  composition laws, not stateful-host or native callback adequacy.
  The independent `HE.RetainedNativeDispatch` factors an executable native
  call into all permitted primitive outcomes, reached worlds and remaining
  language boundaries, with source equivalence in both directions.
  Producer-completed return checks cannot execute new code or change the
  world again. `HE.NativeDispatchFocus` lifts that dispatch through arbitrary
  saved context callers without replacing context identities by snapshots.
  `HERetainedNativeBoundary` makes the actual post-argument cursor and one
  locally certified host reply an instance of the shared protocol. Finished
  replies resume the caller; successful resumable batches enter the language
  boundary in the reached world. Controls exercise two retained caller levels,
  repeated context identity, native errors, duplicate values and alias frames.
  `HE.CompletedNativeShortcut` derives exact row/world preservation for Atom
  and Undefined demands on producer-completed results. Its executable decision
  replaces the canonical boundary batch by returning control only in those
  cases; all other cases retain the canonical post-primitive cursor. The
  shared `HERetainedNativeShortcut` instance preserves and reflects complete
  source observations through arbitrary saved callers, without replaying the
  native operation. Controls distinguish actual queue elimination, omitted
  duplicate results and illegal re-interpretation of completed function data.
  This is the stateful source/canonical-host boundary. Prepared-region
  success and native implementation/codec correspondence remain separate.
* `FirstSuccessCollectedRegions`: completed-frontier normalization transports
  the existing ordered worker/source result relation with its binding theory.
  The source observation names the native three-class output policy explicitly.
* `MutableObservationIdentity`: equality under future permitted writes is
  stronger than equality of current contents. Clearing a cache cannot repair a
  different mutable reference already returned to a retained caller.
* `RetainedTypePayloads`: an executable immutable output grammar earns exact
  interning/materialization and encoded symbol-key source congruence, despite
  hash collisions. Output stability does not establish stability of mutable
  formals or annotations used by inference; native scope admission is separate.
* `HELiteralWorkerDelivery`, `FirstSuccessSquareCollection`: the actual
  first-success worker delivers integer arguments and executes a typed square
  call, retaining its source bindings and resumable return frontier. The two
  preselection frontiers justify the native output policy for this instance.
  Surface superpose/collapse lowering remains distinct from collecting these
  independently earned calls.
* `ChainDeclarationAdmission`, `ChainRegionSourceClosure`: declaration
  metadata and call closure are computed from finite source rows and bodies.
  Unrelated polymorphic declarations need not exclude a supported region;
  reachable unsupported heads do. Native metadata/frame codecs are separate.
* `GroundProtectedRegions`: actual source binding derives stability of a
  ground protected argument, even with interpreted captured values. Per-call
  canonical fallback gives exact recursive runs. Open alias admission and
  substitution-bearing external calls are not covered by this ground rule.
* `TypeDependencyClosure`: source annotation reads, first-local matching,
  substitution, normalization and subtype traversal are composed under
  executable resource-dependency admission. Ordered rows and duplicates are
  retained. The conservative packet gate is not identified with the native
  declaration-index, import, or revision implementation.
* `TypeNormalizationWorklist`: an independently stepped postorder worklist
  implements the recursive normalization specification, with arbitrary saved
  parents. Every partial run retains its residual; exact administrative work
  is two transitions per visited node, excluding primitive-internal work.
  Results of primitives are not re-entered, and short expressions stay opaque.
  Resource-free retained frames permit changing external worlds between
  steps, under the separate primitive output-closure contract.
* `NativeTypingScopeCapture`: the ordinary-atom fresh scan permits unrelated
  mutable data while capturing the rows that can influence type queries.
  A variable-headed subtype row refutes literal-head-only invalidation.
  The corrected projection preserves both actual query packets under equal
  revisions across append histories; native representation and broader edit
  histories still need their adapters.
* `SourceCallAliasTransport`: the actual substitution-bearing PeTTa source
  machine preserves caller equations through all of its transitions. Its
  reached answer packets, including recursive returns, derive ground-fact
  stability and the current-dependency obligation for open claims. The
  native analyzer must establish that obligation; a helper's output flag
  alone does not. The machine's supported source forms remain explicit.
* `SourceGroundEntryFacts`: actual renamed equation-head and list-view
  unification earns the protected ground/uninterpreted marks. The existing
  fact-table merge and subsequent delivered-argument admission use that same
  returned source substitution. Arbitrary compound-body analysis and native
  table codecs remain separate.
* `SubtypeClosureRounds`: repeated whole-row subtype queries are executed
  in ordered rounds, preserving same-round duplicate discoveries. Parent
  indices strictly decrease along ancestry; completed results retain the
  original seed prefix. World-independent queries yield exact identical
  partial and complete runs. No general finite-closure assumption is made.
* `SourceGroundBindFacts`: actual source `let` binding, including quoted and
  list-view patterns, realizes the existing bind-any fact update. Earlier
  ground facts survive through the actual returned branch substitution;
  new flags cannot invent uninterpreted evidence for an interpreted value.
* `SourceContractReturns`: a syntax-derived protected-return obligation
  follows actual saved continuations through calls, effects and alternatives.
  A completed run earns the original ground value once per real answer
  packet, and the separate delivered polymorphic guard preserves that bag.
  Ordinary source body execution is not confused with declaration guards.
* `NativePartialTypeWorld`: the actual partial argument/row demand plans
  preserve both answers and read traces across resource worlds. Reached
  unification derives safe substitutions; normalization agreement is needed
  only at reached resource-free range instances. Missing, malformed and
  completed-negative observations remain distinct.
* `NativeTypeRecursiveWorld`: inferred children and expression operators
  execute the actual recursive request graph. Reached closure-input and
  returned-type safety are derived. Concrete annotation/freshening and
  completed subtype ports yield whole-node world stability at every depth,
  including the full ordered primitive certificate. Unsupported native
  codecs still decline and are not certified by this source instance.
  This uses a fixed-key, fixed-renamer port. `NativeTypeFreshReadControls`
  proves why it does not yet realize repeated native polymorphic reads:
  reusing one subject's variable names couples independent occurrences.
  Resource-world stability is not occurrence-freshness correspondence.
* `NativeTypeScopedWorld`: the same recursive call graph now also has a
  state-threaded interpretation. Actual annotation and subtype-row reads
  allocate distinct injective instances and retain caller/result variables;
  repeated occurrences inside one signature stay linked. Continuation-wise
  query relations derive exact external-world equality of results and final
  supplies, including unfinished runs. The fixed-key counterexample succeeds
  here, including its tuple variant, and a subtype capture control separates
  row variables from input variables. Native frame-identity/primitive codecs
  and full freshening correspondence remain separate obligations.
* `TypeScopeRenaming`, `TypeFreshReadEquivalence`: the actual total unifier
  transports its chosen substitution under permutations, including occurs
  checks and elimination orientation. The atom codec and first-local matcher
  preserve selected state and range readout. Two lawful ordered private
  allocations therefore admit the same call while fixing the public scope.
  `TypeNormalizationNames` adds primitive support/equivariance contracts;
  supported normalization cannot invent a name captured by a later read.
* `CeTTaVariableFreshening`: full-identity ordinal normalization earns the
  stable-base condition for native epoch replacement. Mixed old epochs may
  collapse without that normalization. Allocation failure, low-level ingress
  and allocator ownership remain separate obligations. `CeTTaCurrentFrameCodec`
  derives the current declared 64-bit codec from the existing LayoutCodes and
  generated-expression semantics, including the extra native issuance bound.
  It does not reuse the historical packed-word codec or verify C allocation.
* `SourceCallMetadata`: a completed raw source body lifts above an arbitrary
  saved caller, before that caller is consumed. Its separate typed boundary
  preserves earned ground-polymorphic answers. Closed-range acceptance does
  not establish groundness, and ground-only faithfulness does not certify an
